flowchart LR
    accTitle: Isolated runtime world use cases
    accDescr: One host process owns Aether and lazily creates named AethericFrames. Each frame owns its posture, registries, DevOps control plane, Conduits, and frame-unique objects. Workloads resolve independently, operators attach Rifts to explicitly eligible frames or restore a formation into a target frame, and one frame can be cleaned without collapsing its siblings. Peer Conduit links never cross frame boundaries.

    host["Host application"]
    workload["Independent workloads"]
    operator["Operator / tool / agent"]

    subgraph process["One Python process · one Aether owner"]
        direction TB
        create(["Lazily create named frames"])
        posture(["Bind frame posture<br/>before Spellbooks"])
        isolate(["Isolate owned state<br/>registries · DevOps · Conduits<br/>and unique objects"])
        resolve(["Resolve independent object worlds"])
        resolve_assigned(["Resolve inside an assigned frame"])
        operate(["Operate one named frame"])
        attach(["Attach Rift to an explicitly<br/>eligible named frame"])
        restore(["Restore a formation into<br/>one target frame"])
        cleanup(["Clean one frame without<br/>collapsing sibling worlds"])

        create -.-> posture -.-> isolate -.-> resolve
        resolve_assigned -.-> resolve
        operate -.-> attach
        operate -.-> restore
        operate -.-> cleanup
        isolate -.-> attach
        isolate -.-> restore
        resolve -.-> cleanup
    end

    frame_a["Frame A<br/>own posture + control plane"]
    frame_b["Frame B<br/>own posture + control plane"]
    boundary["Isolation law<br/>unique is per frame<br/>Conduit links are same-frame only"]

    host --> create
    workload --> resolve_assigned
    operator --> operate
    isolate --> frame_a
    isolate --> frame_b
    boundary -.-> frame_a
    boundary -.-> frame_b

